{"reference":"1 Samuel 25","book":"1 Samuel","chapter":25,"status":"pending","sections":[{"kind":"surrounding_passages","title":"Within First Samuel","blocks":[{"id":"block_1","text":"This chapter belongs to the larger movement of 1 Samuel: from Eli's failing priestly house, through Samuel's prophetic leadership and Saul's rejected kingship, to David's anointing, rise, exile, and Saul's death. David's encounter with Nabal and Abigail occurs during the part of the book that follows David's rise while he remains away from settled security.","verse_refs":["1 Samuel 1","1 Samuel 10:1-27","1 Samuel 11:1-15","1 Samuel 12:1-25","1 Samuel 13:1-23","1 Samuel 14:1-52","1 Samuel 15:1-35","1 Samuel 16:1-23","1 Samuel 17:1-58","1 Samuel 18:1-30","1 Samuel 19:1-24","1 Samuel 20:1-42","1 Samuel 21:1-15","1 Samuel 22:1-23","1 Samuel 23:1-29","1 Samuel 24:1-22","1 Samuel 26:1-25","1 Samuel 27:1-12","1 Samuel 28:1-25","1 Samuel 29:1-11","1 Samuel 2:1-36","1 Samuel 30:1-31","1 Samuel 31:1-13","1 Samuel 3:1-21","1 Samuel 4:1-22","1 Samuel 5:1-12","1 Samuel 6:1-21","1 Samuel 7:1-17","1 Samuel 8:1-22","1 Samuel 9:1-27"],"provenance_refs":["reader_path_1_samuel_025_aa11b170ce8638fa67876897"],"confidence":"high","interpretation_level":"fact"}]}],"generated_metadata":null}